// Quiz for the Waterfall topic

::Development models::
_____ is the development model where as each phase completes, the project spills to the next step
{
~Agile
=Waterfall
~Iterative
~V-model
}

::Waterfall model::
Which is NOT an advantage of the waterfall model of development?
{
~It is a simple model that can be followed by developers in developing software.
~All the phases are clearly defined.
~It works well in short projects.
=It does not consume time to implement.
}

::Waterfall model::
In which of these real-world situations would implementing the Waterfall development model NOT be appropriate?
{
=Projects where time is a major factor.
~A human life is at stake and a system failure could result in fatalities.
~Military and aircraft programs where requirements are declared early on and remain constant.
~Projects with an extremely high degree of oversight and/or accountability.
}

::Waterfall model::
The ______ stage of the Waterfall model is where the actual code is written.
{
~Logical Design
~Physical Design
=Implementation
~Maintenance
}